-- California Business and Professions Code, Division 8, Chapter 25.1, the
-- Transparency in Frontier Artificial Intelligence Act (SB 53, Stats. 2025, ch. 138).
-- Critical safety incident reporting: the NOUNS, and nothing else.
--
-- DRAFT. Not for use as advice. No domain expert and no lawyer qualified in
-- California law has read this against the source.
--
-- Seat: a frontier developer (a company), or a developer asking whether it is one.
-- Every fact here is one that developer could state; whether the facts make it a
-- frontier developer, or an event a critical safety incident, is worked out in
-- tfaia-definitions.l4.
-- Source: ../../registers/source-bundle/ca-bpc-div8-ch25-1-tfaia-2026-10.txt

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

§ `Nouns for Chapter 25.1, critical safety incident reporting`

-- One case is one developer and one AI model: the model the incident involves.
-- Training compute is counted in integer or floating-point operations, and includes
-- the original training run and any later fine-tuning, reinforcement learning or other
-- material modification the developer applied (section 22757.11(i)(2)). The last
-- compute figure is about ANY foundation model of the developer's, this one included,
-- because a developer can be a frontier developer through a model other than the one
-- an incident involves.
-- Revenue is in US dollars, for the developer together with its affiliates.
DECLARE `me and my model` HAS
    `the model is an artificial intelligence model`                        IS A BOOLEAN
    `the model was trained on a broad data set`                             IS A BOOLEAN
    `the model is designed for generality of output`                        IS A BOOLEAN
    `the model is adaptable to a wide range of distinctive tasks`           IS A BOOLEAN
    `I have trained, or initiated the training of, the model`               IS A BOOLEAN
    `the operations used to train the model so far`                         IS A NUMBER
    `the most operations I have used or intend to use to train any foundation model I have trained or begun to train` IS A NUMBER
    `the annual gross revenues of me and my affiliates in the preceding calendar year` IS A NUMBER

-- What the model did, in the words of section 22757.11(c)(1)(A) to (C).
DECLARE `what the model did` IS ONE OF
    `none of the three kinds of conduct`
    `provided expert-level assistance in the creation or release of a chemical, biological, radiological, or nuclear weapon`
    `engaged, with no meaningful human oversight, intervention, or supervision, in a cyberattack or in conduct that would be murder, assault, extortion, or theft if committed by a human`
    `evaded the control of its frontier developer or user`

-- The event, as the developer knows it. Counts of people and dollars are for the
-- one incident; the dollar figure leaves out any loss of value of equity, which
-- section 22757.16 says is not damage to or loss of property.
DECLARE `the incident as I know it` HAS
    `there was unauthorized access to, modification of, or exfiltration of the model weights` IS A BOOLEAN
    `that access, modification, or exfiltration resulted in death or bodily injury` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the model's conduct`                                                    IS A `what the model did`
    `the model materially contributed to the deaths, injuries, or damage`    IS A BOOLEAN
    `the deaths, injuries, or damage arose from a single incident`           IS A BOOLEAN
    `the number of people who died or were seriously injured`               IS A NUMBER
    `the dollars of damage to, or loss of, property`                         IS A NUMBER
    `the harm came from information the model output that is otherwise publicly accessible in a substantially similar form from a source other than a foundation model` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the harm came from lawful activity of the federal government`           IS A BOOLEAN
    `there was a loss of control of the model`                               IS A BOOLEAN
    `the loss of control caused death or bodily injury`                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `the model used deceptive techniques against me to subvert my controls or monitoring` IS A BOOLEAN
    `that happened in an evaluation designed to elicit that behavior`        IS A BOOLEAN
    `that behavior demonstrates materially increased catastrophic risk`      IS A BOOLEAN

-- The four kinds of critical safety incident, section 22757.11(d)(1) to (4).
DECLARE `a kind of critical safety incident` IS ONE OF
    `kind 1, unauthorized access to, modification of, or exfiltration of model weights resulting in death or bodily injury`
    `kind 2, harm resulting from the materialization of a catastrophic risk`
    `kind 3, loss of control of a frontier model causing death or bodily injury`
    `kind 4, deceptive subversion of the developer's controls or monitoring`

-- Where I stand on reporting: when I discovered the incident, and the facts that turn
-- the chapter, or the federal route of section 22757.13(i), on or off for me.
DECLARE `my reporting position` HAS
    `the date I discovered the critical safety incident`                     IS A DATE
    `I have discovered that the incident poses an imminent risk of death or serious physical injury` IS A BOOLEAN
    `my declaration under section 22757.13(i) is in effect`                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the chapter is in force and not preempted as applied to me`             IS A BOOLEAN
    `a contract between a federal government entity and me strictly conflicts with the reporting duty` IS A BOOLEAN

-- The four things the Office of Emergency Services' mechanism takes, section
-- 22757.13(a)(1) to (4).
DECLARE `an item of a critical safety incident report` IS ONE OF
    `item 1, the date of the critical safety incident`
    `item 2, the reasons the incident qualifies as a critical safety incident`
    `item 3, a short and plain statement describing the critical safety incident`
    `item 4, whether the incident was associated with internal use of a frontier model`

-- What I failed to do, for the penalty question (section 22757.15).
DECLARE `a failure of mine` IS ONE OF
    `I failed to report a critical safety incident to the Office of Emergency Services within 15 days`
    `I failed to disclose an imminent-risk incident within 24 hours`
